  "id": "symbolic-play",
  "term": "symbolic play",
  "definition": "Symbolic play is play in which a child uses things, actions, or roles to stand for other objects, events, or people. It reflects developing representational thinking, including understanding that a symbol can have a meaning that is different from the symbol itself, and it is an important part of early development.",
